If clash has the SAME baseUrl → loop doesn't run → returns the same name → `_landEntry` updates in place. That's the deliberate re-auth semantics for ChatGPT/AIIN (matches PR description: "ChatGPT/AIIN/Copilot by (name + endpoint)").

Hmm, but there's a subtle behavior difference vs the flutter_app: the app creates a NEW entry `u@aiin.by-2` even for the same endpoint+name (since its loop matches name AND baseUrl → also same → wait no). Re-read the app's loop:

```dart
while (registry.providers.any((p) => p.name == name && p.baseUrl == baseUrl)) {
  name = '$identity-${suffix++}';
}
```

The app SUFFIXES when name+baseUrl match (creating u@aiin.by-2 for a second connect of the same account? Hmm — but the app has a separate reauthenticateFor path that refreshes in place). Actually in the app's fresh-connect path, a same name+endpoint match creates `u@aiin.by-2` (new entry), while in fa_ui it updates the existing entry in place. This is a documented divergence ("interpretation note: fa_ui defaults reuse-on-match for re-auth"), disclosed in the PR description. The flutter_app keeps its richer flows. OK — disclosed; not a bug per se, but worth noting? It's disclosed explicitly. Skip.

3. The AIIN base URL question. Let me check `aiinDefaultChatBaseUrl`.

